{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"55ef1236762c9810","name":"card_unit_beaufighter_vi_f","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/CovertOp/units/card_unit_beaufighter_vi_f","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BEAUFIGHTER VI F","text":"British air units you deploy get +2+2.","flavorText":"The Bristol Beaufighter was a British multi-role aircraft introduced into service in 1940 during the Battle of Britain and used by the Royal Air Force (RAF), the Commonwealth Air Forces and the United States Army Air Forces (USAAF) throughout WWII. The Beaufighter was originally designed as a heavy fighter and proved to be a very effective night fighter as it was able to carry heavy armament and early airborne interception radar without it affecting its performance. The Beaufighter VI variant was introduced in 1942, and the Beaufighter VI F variant was equipped with AI Mark VIII radar which greatly enhanced its performance as a night fighter. However, in late 1942 the faster de Havilland Mosquito became the main night fighter, but the heavier Beaufighter made a valuable contribution in other areas such as anti-shipping, long range interdiction and ground attack roles, and it came to great use in every major theater of operations.","faction":"Britain","type":"fighter","rarity":"Unique","cost":5,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_beaufighter_vi_f","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_beaufighter_vi_f_title","SourceString":"BEAUFIGHTER VI F","LocalizedString":"BEAUFIGHTER VI F"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":4,"defense":5,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_beaufighter_vi_f_text","SourceString":"British air units you deploy get +2+2.","LocalizedString":"British air units you deploy get +2+2."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_beaufighter_vi_f_history","SourceString":"The Bristol Beaufighter was a British multi-role aircraft introduced into service in 1940 during the Battle of Britain and used by the Royal Air Force (RAF), the Commonwealth Air Forces and the United States Army Air Forces (USAAF) throughout WWII. The Beaufighter was originally designed as a heavy fighter and proved to be a very effective night fighter as it was able to carry heavy armament and early airborne interception radar without it affecting its performance. The Beaufighter VI variant was introduced in 1942, and the Beaufighter VI F variant was equipped with AI Mark VIII radar which greatly enhanced its performance as a night fighter. However, in late 1942 the faster de Havilland Mosquito became the main night fighter, but the heavier Beaufighter made a valuable contribution in other areas such as anti-shipping, long range interdiction and ground attack roles, and it came to great use in every major theater of operations.","LocalizedString":"The Bristol Beaufighter was a British multi-role aircraft introduced into service in 1940 during the Battle of Britain and used by the Royal Air Force (RAF), the Commonwealth Air Forces and the United States Army Air Forces (USAAF) throughout WWII. The Beaufighter was originally designed as a heavy fighter and proved to be a very effective night fighter as it was able to carry heavy armament and early airborne interception radar without it affecting its performance. The Beaufighter VI variant was introduced in 1942, and the Beaufighter VI F variant was equipped with AI Mark VIII radar which greatly enhanced its performance as a night fighter. However, in late 1942 the faster de Havilland Mosquito became the main night fighter, but the heavier Beaufighter made a valuable contribution in other areas such as anti-shipping, long range interdiction and ground attack roles, and it came to great use in every major theater of operations."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","EffectType":"